sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch12-14> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Insofar as forms depend on physical forces and their variations on simple quantitative changes in those forces, similarity of form cannot safely be taken as evidence of consanguinity, and the link between classification and phylogeny must be revised.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Forms set by physical forces undermine inference of kinship from similarity";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XII, “The Spiral Shells of the Foraminifera”; topic “Physical explanation versus phylogeny”. Scope: Foraminifera and other organisms whose form is governed by physical forces"
}
